<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's LPMO to seek 10,860T of frozen beef.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's LPMO to seek 10,860T of frozen beef.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Livestock Products Marketing Organisation said on Friday it will hold tenders to buy 10,860 tonnes of frozen beef at 2 p.m. (0500 GMT) on October 18.  </p>
<p>An LPMO official said acceptable origins were set for U.S., Canada, Ireland, Sweden, Denmark, Japan, Taiwan, New Zealand, Australia, Finland, Mexico and Netherlands.</p>
<p>If LPMO passes on the tenders in whole or partially on Friday due to high prices, it will re-invite the tenders on October 22.</p>
<p>Arrivals were set for Seoul, Pusan, Daegu and Naju.  </p>
<p>Details for the tenders are as follow:</p>
